<section id="help" class="help" aria-label="How to print">
    <div class="help-top">
        <h2>How to print</h2>
        <button type="button" class="help-close" aria-label="Close help" title="Close" @ref="_close" @onclick="Close">×</button>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h3>In two colours</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Click <b>Download 3MF</b>.</li>
            <li>Double-click the file to open it in Bambu Studio.</li>
            <li>Base and Letters (and Back text, if you added one) come in as parts. Choose a filament for each.</li>
            <li>Slice and print.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h3>Good to know</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>An STL has no colours. Use 3MF to keep the parts.</li>
            <li><b>Separate objects</b> (next to Download 3MF) makes every name its own object, so you can move it alone in Bambu Studio. <b>One object</b> keeps them together.</li>
            <li>Arrange › <b>Fill the bed</b> packs the names tightly and turns some sideways to fit more. When a bed is full it starts another, and each bed becomes its own plate in Bambu Studio. Set Plate width and depth to your printer.</li>
            <li>The colours on this page are for the preview only. The real ones are the filaments you pick.</li>
            <li>The grams shown assume solid PETG, so they are an upper limit.</li>
            <li>A cup marker appears upside down and mirrored, because it prints name side down with no supports. Do not flip it.</li>
            <li>Hanukkah candle: the name runs along the candle, first letter by the flame. Long names make the candle and letters smaller together, down to Smallest letters. Names with tall or deep letters (ל, ק) come out a little smaller so they stay inside the candle. Ring position puts the hole in a tab at the bottom, just under the flame, in a loop above the flame, or leaves it out. Back text (optional) is the same on every candle: it is set into the bottom, flush, as its own part (filament 3), and reads correctly when you turn the candle over. Flip back text turns it end over end. The longer of name and back text sets the candle's length.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h3>Your data</h3>
        <p>Names, settings and uploaded fonts stay in this browser. Nothing is sent anywhere.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="credits">
        <h3>Credits</h3>
        <p>Fonts: Gan CLM (GNU GPL v2), Chewy (Apache 2.0), the others SIL Open Font License 1.1. <a href="https://github.com/eladgl-dot/3d-name-tag-generator/tree/main/assets/fonts/licences" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full licence texts</a></p>
        <p>Libraries: three.js (MIT), Clipper2 (Boost), LibTessDotNet (SGI Free Software License B), SixLabors.Fonts (Apache 2.0).</p>
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    [Parameter] public EventCallback Close { get; set; }

    ElementReference _close;

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender) await _close.FocusAsync();
    }
}
